@startuml Solver Begins Work
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam sequence {
  ArrowColor #555555
  LifeLineBorderColor #999999
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #FAFAFA
  ParticipantBorderColor #444444
  ActorBackgroundColor #FAFAFA
  FontName Helvetica
}
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFF8E1
skinparam noteBorderColor #D4AF37

title Solver Begins Resolving an Assigned Incident

actor Solver
participant "Browser\n(incident page)" as Browser
participant "nginx" as Nginx
participant "Django view\nincident_transition" as View
participant "Transition rules" as Rules
database "PostgreSQL" as DB

== Open the incident ==
Solver -> Browser : Click incident from list
Browser -> Nginx : GET /incidents/12/
Nginx -> View : forward request
View -> DB : SELECT incident 12
DB --> View : incident row
View -> View : Verify user is a solver\nand incident is assigned to\none of their teams
View -> DB : SELECT updates for incident 12
DB --> View : timeline rows
View --> Browser : Render incident page\nwith allowed next actions
Browser --> Solver : Show ticket, timeline,\nand "Acknowledge" button

== Acknowledge ==
Solver -> Browser : Click "Acknowledge"
Browser -> Nginx : POST /incidents/12/transition/\nnew_status=acknowledged
Nginx -> View : forward request
View -> DB : SELECT incident 12
DB --> View : incident row (status = open)
View -> View : Verify solver role and\nteam assignment again
View -> Rules : is_allowed(open -> acknowledged)
Rules --> View : allowed

View -> DB : UPDATE incident\nSET status = acknowledged,\nassigned_to = solver
View -> DB : INSERT IncidentUpdate\n(incident, author, type = status_change,\nold = open, new = acknowledged, timestamp)
DB --> View : committed

View --> Browser : 302 redirect to /incidents/12/\nwith success message
Browser -> Nginx : GET /incidents/12/
Nginx -> View : forward request
View -> DB : SELECT incident and updates
DB --> View : rows
View --> Browser : Render page
Browser --> Solver : "Ticket #12 acknowledged"\ntimeline shows the change\nnext action is "Start work"

== Rejected transition ==
Solver -> Browser : Attempt "Resolve" from Acknowledged
Browser -> Nginx : POST /incidents/12/transition/\nnew_status=resolved
Nginx -> View : forward request
View -> Rules : is_allowed(acknowledged -> resolved)
Rules --> View : rejected: must be In Progress first
View --> Browser : 302 redirect with error message
Browser --> Solver : "Cannot move from Acknowledged\nto Resolved. Start work first."

note over View, DB
  The status update and the timeline insert run in one
  database transaction. Either both succeed or neither does.
end note

@enduml
